WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.567
-Our next guest is a talented
actress you know

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:04.300
from films such
as "In the Heights"

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:05.534
and the Scream franchise.

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:08.133
She stars in the latest
installment, "Scream VI."

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:09.234
It should be
in theaters everywhere

00:00:09.234 --> 00:00:11.300
this Friday, March 10th.
Let's take a look.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.934
[ Suspenseful music plays ]
[ Thudding ]

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:14.901
-Hey!

00:00:14.901 --> 00:00:16.868
[ Vehicle horns blaring ]

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:19.634
Don't worry.
I got you.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.934
-Are you kidding me?
-You have a better idea?

00:00:23.934 --> 00:00:25.000
[ Thudding ]
-No.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:31.267
♪♪

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:32.467
[ Thudding ]
-Come on.

00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:33.734
Eyes on me.

00:00:33.734 --> 00:00:34.667
Keep your eyes on me.

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:36.234
-Go!
[ Thudding ]

00:00:38.234 --> 00:00:39.634
-[ Sobbing ]
-Oh, my God.

00:00:39.634 --> 00:00:41.167
-I got you.
I got you.

00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:44.100
[ Thudding ]
-[ Grunts ]

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.167 --> 00:00:48.534
-Please welcome to the show
Melissa Barrera, everybody.

00:00:48.534 --> 00:00:50.534
[ Band plays mellow funk ]
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:50.534 --> 00:00:59.434
♪♪

00:00:59.434 --> 00:01:08.234
♪♪

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.000
Welcome!
I'm so happy to have you here!

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.934
-I'm so happy. This is my first
late night show ever.

00:01:12.934 --> 00:01:15.467
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Well, you're doing a great job.

00:01:15.467 --> 00:01:16.834
[ Whistling ]
Usually --

00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:18.934
Usually, first timers
just wander off

00:01:18.934 --> 00:01:20.434
and you made it right over here.

00:01:20.434 --> 00:01:23.234
-Well, so far, I didn't trip,
which was what I was afraid of.

00:01:23.234 --> 00:01:24.968
-I remember the first time
I was on a talk show,

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:26.701
that was my biggest concern,
was just like

00:01:26.701 --> 00:01:28.467
making it fully
to the couch okay.

00:01:28.467 --> 00:01:30.133
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah. So, so far, so good.
-You're off to a great start.

00:01:30.133 --> 00:01:31.367
Off and running.
-Thanks.

00:01:31.367 --> 00:01:32.667
-Congratulations on the movie.

00:01:32.667 --> 00:01:35.267
I know you had the premiere here
and was it fantastic?

00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:36.901
-It was incredible.
It was last night

00:01:36.901 --> 00:01:41.033
at the Lincoln Center AMC
and it was so magical.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:43.901
We didn't get a premiere for the
last one because, you know,

00:01:43.901 --> 00:01:45.701
Omicron.
-Right, right.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.701 --> 00:01:48.701
-And so this was like
a double whammy premiere

00:01:48.701 --> 00:01:51.567
and it felt big and it was
wonderful and magical.

00:01:51.567 --> 00:01:53.367
-And, you know, I've lived
in the city for, you know,

00:01:53.367 --> 00:01:54.467
over 20 years and I will say,

00:01:54.467 --> 00:01:55.834
when a big horror movie
comes out,

00:01:55.834 --> 00:01:58.133
there is no more fun place
to see it than Times Square.

00:01:58.133 --> 00:02:00.968
[ Laughter ]
I mean that genuinely,
like those crowds

00:02:00.968 --> 00:02:03.567
are exactly the kind of crowds
that have the sort of fun

00:02:03.567 --> 00:02:05.434
that you're supposed
to have at movies like this.

00:02:05.434 --> 00:02:09.300
-I mean, horror is such a like
a communal experience.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:12.267
You need to see it with people
because people are shouting

00:02:12.267 --> 00:02:14.801
and yelling at the screen
and gasping

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:17.067
and it's contagious
and it's fun to do that.

00:02:17.067 --> 00:02:19.133
-This is you
with some of your costars.

00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:21.234
You all look wonderful,
but this is even more exciting.

00:02:21.234 --> 00:02:25.300
This is your family joined you
and they were all there.

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:27.434
And were they so proud?
Were they so happy?

00:02:27.434 --> 00:02:32.100
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Yeah. That's my sister Rossana;
my mom;

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:34.601
my husband;
and my baby sister, Mayela.

00:02:34.601 --> 00:02:36.067
And my other sister, Regina,

00:02:36.067 --> 00:02:37.334
who lives in Spain,
couldn't be here.

00:02:37.334 --> 00:02:39.634
But to me,
the most important thing

00:02:39.634 --> 00:02:41.634
is sharing my work
with my family,

00:02:41.634 --> 00:02:44.267
so, the fact that they all
made it out was really special.

00:02:44.267 --> 00:02:46.300
-Now, of course, anybody
who's watching a "Scream" movie

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:47.834
is trying to guess
who is Ghostface,

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:49.000
who's behind the mask.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:50.567
Your family,
did they participate in that?

00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:51.934
Were they trying
to figure it out?

00:02:51.934 --> 00:02:54.133
They do, because I don't
tell them anything.
-Really?

00:02:54.133 --> 00:02:55.133
Do they try
to get it out of you

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:56.434
or they know
that it's pointless?

00:02:56.434 --> 00:02:57.767
-Every day, they try.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:02:57.767 --> 00:03:01.100
[ Laughter ]
They try to like catch me
off-guard.

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:02.834
But I don't --

00:03:02.834 --> 00:03:05.734
I am really bad
when I start oversharing,

00:03:05.734 --> 00:03:08.000
so, I just say
I'm not going to tell anyone.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:13.000
And that means not even my mom,
not my husband, not anyone, so.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.501
They get to participate
in the whodunit mystery

00:03:15.501 --> 00:03:18.501
and they get to --
And I love watching them

00:03:18.501 --> 00:03:20.367
watch the movie
for the first time

00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:24.534
and they're like real reactions
and it's really -- it's cool.

00:03:24.534 --> 00:03:26.601
-That's good. And did any
of them correctly guess?

00:03:26.601 --> 00:03:28.367
Did they admit
to you afterwards?
-No, they did not, yeah.

00:03:28.367 --> 00:03:29.501
-Alright. That's even more fun.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:30.701
[ Laughter ]
It is fun.

00:03:30.701 --> 00:03:33.033
-There is a scene,
a fantastic scene --

00:03:33.033 --> 00:03:34.501
This movie takes place
in New York City,

00:03:34.501 --> 00:03:36.100
which is a first
for the Scream franchise.

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:38.501
There's this very scary scene
that takes place on the subway.

00:03:38.501 --> 00:03:41.734
-I really apologize
to all subway users

00:03:41.734 --> 00:03:43.000
[ Laughter ]
in New York City.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:45.434
-Now, I will say
it's bad enough,

00:03:45.434 --> 00:03:46.801
even without the slashers...

00:03:46.801 --> 00:03:48.167
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:03:48.167 --> 00:03:50.100
-...like without Ghostface,
like it wasn't like people

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:52.701
were like, "Oh, the subways were
great until that."

00:03:52.701 --> 00:03:54.601
[ Laughter ]
-I know.

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:57.300
-But was it fun to shoot it here
in New York

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:58.501
and to bring the franchise here?

00:03:58.501 --> 00:03:59.934
-We did shoot in New York.

00:03:59.934 --> 00:04:02.000
-Well, that is heartbreaking.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:03.767
[ Laughter ]
-I know.
-I guess that makes sense.

00:04:03.767 --> 00:04:05.133
I didn't see Ghostface
running around.

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:07.200
[ Laughter ]
-I know.
Well, have you seen him like

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:09.968
standing on corners creepily
as part of like the marketing?

00:04:09.968 --> 00:04:11.667
-That's not okay, by the way.
-I know!

00:04:11.667 --> 00:04:13.033
[ Laughter ]
I know it's not!
-Yeah.

00:04:13.033 --> 00:04:15.634
-I actually am not sure
if it's part of the marketing

00:04:15.634 --> 00:04:18.801
or if it's just someone decided
to do that and made the news.

00:04:18.801 --> 00:04:20.133
-Like there's
a Times Square Elmo,

00:04:20.133 --> 00:04:21.901
but that's not "Sesame Street."
-Yeah.

00:04:21.901 --> 00:04:24.300
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:26.901
-That's not a reminder
to tune in.

00:04:26.901 --> 00:04:29.601
-But they built --
So, in Mont--

00:04:29.601 --> 00:04:31.100
We shot in Montreal.

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:33.300
They had a whole soundstage

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:36.934
and they built a subway
with a station

00:04:36.934 --> 00:04:39.200
and the train would go in
and out of the station,

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:41.567
inside a studio.
It was mind-blowing.

00:04:41.567 --> 00:04:43.100
And it was dirty, too.

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:45.501
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:04:45.501 --> 00:04:46.901
-Very accurate.

00:04:46.901 --> 00:04:49.501
[ Laughter ]
-Now, I remember

00:04:49.501 --> 00:04:52.234
when I saw the first "Scream"
movie in theaters --

00:04:52.234 --> 00:04:54.567
I know I'm older than you --
I Googled it.

00:04:54.567 --> 00:04:55.701
That's how I know. I didn't --

00:04:55.701 --> 00:04:57.167
[ Laughter ]
Like at first, I was like,

00:04:57.167 --> 00:04:58.701
"Are we the same age?"
But no.

00:04:58.701 --> 00:05:01.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:04.467
So, I'm assuming you did not see
the first one in theaters,

00:05:04.467 --> 00:05:06.901
but you must've seen --
remember the first time

00:05:06.901 --> 00:05:08.434
you saw the "Scream" movie.
-I do remember.

00:05:08.434 --> 00:05:11.267
I didn't see it when it came out
because I was six, but I --

00:05:11.267 --> 00:05:14.133
[ Laughter ]
-Don't. It's not important
how old you are.

00:05:14.133 --> 00:05:16.334
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.334 --> 00:05:18.400
-I did -- I was obsessed
with horror movies

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:21.434
when I was like 10, 11, 12.

00:05:21.434 --> 00:05:23.467
And I wasn't allowed
to watch horror movies,

00:05:23.467 --> 00:05:26.133
so, I would either lock myself
in my room

00:05:26.133 --> 00:05:29.033
or, at sleepovers
with my friends,

00:05:29.033 --> 00:05:32.767
watch "Scream"
and "Final Destination"

00:05:32.767 --> 00:05:34.267
and, you know, "I Know What You
Did Last Summer"

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:36.534
and all those obsessively.

00:05:36.534 --> 00:05:38.334
I'm kind of a masochist that way

00:05:38.334 --> 00:05:41.234
[ Laughter ]
because I love
watching horror movies

00:05:41.234 --> 00:05:42.901
and I cannot sleep at night,

00:05:42.901 --> 00:05:45.400
but I kind of love that,
weirdly, yes.

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:48.067
-Do you remember the first one
that really scared you,

00:05:48.067 --> 00:05:49.834
was it one of the --
-Yes, "Chucky."

00:05:49.834 --> 00:05:51.434
[ Laughter ]
-"Chucky," yeah.

00:05:51.434 --> 00:05:52.567
-Yeah.
-"Chucky's" not okay,
either, yeah.

00:05:52.567 --> 00:05:55.167
[ Laughter ]
-It was not okay.

00:05:55.167 --> 00:05:57.834
I specifically remember
this scene where he's --

00:05:57.834 --> 00:06:00.634
It's like a back --
the back of like a big like

00:06:00.634 --> 00:06:02.767
moving truck or something
and he's --

00:06:02.767 --> 00:06:07.100
like the little doll
is holding someone hostage --

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:09.167
however that happens --
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.167 --> 00:06:12.133
and someone's following in a car
or running or something

00:06:12.133 --> 00:06:14.334
and the little doll
just flips them off.

00:06:14.334 --> 00:06:15.267
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.267 --> 00:06:16.801
And it's actually hilarious,

00:06:16.801 --> 00:06:18.534
but it was so scary
to me at the time.

00:06:18.534 --> 00:06:22.167
[ Laughter ]
-I like that,
of all of Chucky's crimes,

00:06:22.167 --> 00:06:24.267
-I know!
-the one you couldn't stand for
is rudeness.

00:06:24.267 --> 00:06:26.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:26.767 --> 00:06:29.067
-That's what I remember.

00:06:29.067 --> 00:06:31.467
-I think that says
you're a very polite person.

00:06:31.467 --> 00:06:34.400
Of the many things we should
take away, it's that.

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:35.834
Hey, congratulations
on the movie.

00:06:35.834 --> 00:06:37.234
It was so delightful
to have you here.

00:06:37.234 --> 00:06:38.801
You're a pro.
Let me just tell you,
-Thank you.

00:06:38.801 --> 00:06:40.133
Thank you so much.
-You're a pro at being
a talk show guest.

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:42.067
[ Cheering and applause ]
Melissa Barrera, everybody.

00:06:42.067 --> 00:06:44.300
"Scream VI" will be in theaters
everywhere this Friday.

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:45.968
We'll be right back
with Margaret Atwood.

